FONTS EMBEDDED IN THE PDFs
--------------------------

The PDFs this repository builds embed font subsets. The fonts are the four that
typst bundles; docs/theme/pack.typ is restricted to them and the build passes
`--ignore-system-fonts`, which is what makes a PDF built on a laptop
byte-identical to one built in CI. Because the subsets are embedded in a
distributed artifact, their licences are recorded here rather than left to the
renderer.

Verified 2026-09-15 against the NOTICE file of github.com/typst/typst-assets at
commit 94dcb990edb36311ef85162baa26e4a8205e0bf0, which is the repository that
ships the font files.

  Libertinus Serif                SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1
    Copyright (c) 2012-2024 The Libertinus Project Authors, with Reserved Font
    Names "Linux Libertine", "Biolinum", "STIX Fonts".
    Used for body text and headings.

  New Computer Modern             GUST Font License, Version 1.0
    Applies to every NewComputerModern face except NewCM10-Regular, which
    upstream distributes under the NewComputerModern License with a
    Distribution Exception. Present because typst bundles it; not selected by
    this theme.

  New Computer Modern Math        as above
    Present because typst bundles it; this theme sets no mathematics.

  DejaVu Sans Mono                Bitstream Vera Fonts Copyright
    Fonts are (c) 2003 Bitstream, Inc. DejaVu changes are in the public domain.
    "Bitstream Vera" is a trademark of Bitstream, Inc.; the DejaVu faces are
    renamed precisely so that the trademark condition is met.
    Used for code, inline literals and the revision hash on each cover.

The OFL's requirement that font software "must not be sold by itself" and the
GUST licence's conditions both concern redistribution of the *font software*.
Neither restricts a document produced with the fonts: the OFL says so in terms
("The requirement for fonts to remain under this license does not apply to any
document created using the Font Software").


BUILD-TIME DEPENDENCIES
-----------------------

  pandoc                          GPL-2.0-or-later
    github.com/jgm/pandoc. Invoked as an external program by
    scripts/build-docs.py. No pandoc source or object code is linked into or
    distributed with this project, so its copyleft terms do not reach the
    contents of this repository or the PDFs it produces.

  typst                           Apache-2.0
    github.com/typst/typst, with bundled assets from typst/typst-assets, also
    Apache-2.0. Invoked as pandoc's PDF engine.

  poppler (pdftotext, pdfinfo)    GPL-2.0-or-later
    poppler.freedesktop.org. Invoked as an external program by the overflow
    check and the reproducibility fingerprint. Same reasoning as pandoc.

  PyYAML                          MIT
  jsonschema                      MIT
    Installed into a local .venv by `make deps`, never vendored. These are the
    only two Python packages the checks require; scripts/doctor.sh and
    scripts/link-check.sh deliberately require neither, so that a broken Python
    can still be diagnosed and links can still be checked.


